Cook County, Illinois
 
ORDINANCE NO.25-16-56
 
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CERTAIN PROVISIONS OF THE
OAK LAWN VILLAGE CODE PERTAINING TO
THE ARTS AND EVENTS COMMISSION
 
WHEREAS, Section 6(a) of Article VII of the 1970 Constitution of the State of
Illinois provides that any municipality which has a population of more than
25,000 is a home rule unit, and the Village of Oak Lawn, Cook County, Illinois,
with a population in excess of 25,000 is, therefore, a home rule unit and,
pursuant to the provisions of said Section 6(a) of Article VII, may exercise
any power and perform any function pertaining to its government and affairs,
including, but not limited to, the power to tax and to incur debt; and
 
WHEREAS, the President and Board of Trustees of the Village of Oak Lawn have
previously established the Oak Lawn Arts and Events Commission, as set forth in
Title 2, Chapter 21, of the Oak Lawn Village Code; and
 
   WHEREAS, the President and Board of Trustees have determined that it is in
the best interests of the residents of the Village of Oak Lawn to amend certain
provisions of the Oak Lawn Village Code related to the currently existing Arts
and Events Commission;
 
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED BY THE VILLAGE PRESIDENT AND BOARD OF TRUSTEES
OF THE VILLAGE OF OAK LAWN, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS, IN THE EXERCISE OF ITS HOME
RULE POWERS, AS FOLLOWS:
 
   SECTION 1:   That the foregoing recitals shall be and are hereby
incorporated as findings of fact as if said recitals were fully set forth
herein.
   SECTION 2:   That the Arts and Events Commission is hereby renamed to the
Oak Lawn Special Events Commission, and the title of Title 2, Chapter 21, of
the Oak Lawn Village Code is hereby amended accordingly.
   SECTION 3:   That Title 2, Chapter 21, Section 1 of the Oak Lawn Village
Code is hereby amended to read in its entirety as follows (additions to
existing text marked with underlined text ; deletions to existing text marked
using strikethrough ):
2-21-1: DEFINITIONS:
    A.   The terms "arts" and "art" as used in this section include, but are
not limited to, creative writing, dance, film/video, music, theater, visual
arts, crafts, performing arts, spoken word, environmental arts, multimedia
arts, architectural arts, landscape architecture, and emerging media.
    B.    The term s " special  event" and " special  events" as used in this
section shall mean community based temporary aggregation of people or attracts
  attractions  for a common purpose, including but not limited to holidays,
festivals, street fairs, arts and craft shows, carnivals, circuses, rallies,
public entertainment, or other similar events or attractions.
 
SECTION 4: That Title 2, Chapter 21, Section 2 of the Oak Lawn Village Code is
hereby amended to read in its entirety as follows (additions to existing text
marked with underlined text ; deletions to existing text marked using
strikethrough ):
2-21-2: COMMISSION CREATED, APPOINTMENT, MEMBER- SHIP:
There is hereby created and established a fourteen (14)   seven (7)  member
Village of Oak Lawn Arts and Events   Special Events  Commission, hereinafter
referred to as the "commission", whereby the President shall appoint two
(2) one (1)  member s and each Village Trustee shall appoint two (2)   one (1)
member s from their own district. Members shall be chosen from a diverse range
of backgrounds, occupations, and artistic venues, with the intention of
reflecting the full diversity of the Oak Lawn arts community. If a vacancy
exists following the failure and/or refusal by a Village Trustee to appoint a
member by October 1 of the calendar year , an appointment shall be made by a
recommendation from the President   BOT Events Liaison  with approval of the
majority of the Village Board.
 
The President and Board of Trustees may compel attendance of any absent member
and may remove any such member from said Commission if that member misses three
(3) consecutive meetings. The removal shall be initiated by the President and
subject to the confirmation of such removal by the advice and consent of the
Village Board.
 
Each member of the Commission shall receive a sum of one hundred dollars
($100.00) per meeting for every meeting attended, or such prorated portion
thereof as shall represent the time served in a given calendar year, with a
minimum annual remuneration of $500.00 per member if the member attends 70% or
more of all properly posted meetings. This remuneration is intended to cover
normal and necessary expenses of the member. Additional or unusual expenses may
be covered as budgeted upon receipt of proper evidence of expenditure and
approval by this Commission.
 
      A.   Regular Meetings: Meetings shall be held at every month on the 3rd
Wednesday of said Month, except for the months of December ,   and  January
February  with a maximum of ten (10)   nine (9)  meetings a year, except that
the Commission may, by rule, provide for changing the date for seasonal reasons
of in the event there is no pending business.
 
     B.   Special Meetings: Special meetings may be called by the chairman or
by any three (3) members of the Commission.
   
C.   Open To The Public: All meetings of the Arts and Events Commission and its
committees shall be open meetings as required under the applicable statutes of
the State of Illinois and codes of the Village.
 
SECTION 5: That Title 2, Chapter 21, Section 3 of the Oak Lawn Village Code is
hereby amended to read in its entirety as follows (additions to existing text
marked with underlined text ; deletions to existing text marked using
strikethrough ):
2-21-3: TERMS OF OFFICE:
All appointments, except to vacancies, shall begin on September 1 of the
calendar year. Members of the Arts and Events Special Events  Commission
serving as of the effective date hereof shall serve until the end of the term
to which appointed and until their successors are named and qualified.
Effective September 1, 2019, a full term shall be four (4) years and terms
shall be staggered so not more than eight (8) four (4)  expire each year. Such
staggered terms shall coincide with District 1, 3, and 5 appointees to expire
opposite years of District 2, 4, and 6 appointees. For purposes of this
Chapter, such appointments for District 2, 4, and 6 beginning on September 1,
2019, shall have initial term limit to end in calendar year 2021 so as to
initiate such staggered terms. Effective November 30, 2025, the terms of seven
(7) current members of the Commission shall end.  One (1) commissioner from
each district and one (1) commissioner appointed by the Village President shall
either voluntarily resign from the Commission or be removed by written notice
from the party that appointed them.
 
SECTION 6:   That Title 2, Chapter 21, Section 6 of the Oak Lawn Village Code
is hereby amended to read in its entirety as follows (additions to existing
text marked with underlined text ; deletions to existing text marked using
strikethrough ):
2-21-6: POWERS AND DUTIES:
The commission shall adopt its rules of procedure for whatever regular and
special meetings are deemed by the commission to be advisable and necessary to
the fulfillment of the duties of the commission. Nothing in this chapter shall
be construed as vesting legislative or budgetary discretion or power in the
commission.
The duties and responsibilities of the commission shall be to research issues
related to special events and to make recommendations to the President and
Board of Trustees, to make recommendations as to where, when and under what
conditions and circumstances parades and special events may be held in the
village, and to perform such other duties as may be requested from time to time
by the President and Board of Trustees and/or the BOT Events Liaison.may
include, but not be limited to, the following:
    A.   To explore and recommend to the village president, board of trustees,
village staff, and other groups ways to further the development of, and
interest in the arts, strengthen Oak Lawn's cultural awareness, ways to expand
opportunities for artistic expressions special events, and offer advice on
relevant village projects.
    B.   To propose to the president and board of trustees an annual public
arts special events program plan that identifies specific program goals of the
year, means of achievement, proposed expenditures, sources of supplemental
revenue, schedule of execution, necessary resources and responsibilities, and
implementation of a plan to address stated goals.
    C.   To recommend to the president and board of trustees policies regarding
the selection of special events.proposed public arts projects such as the
involvement of artists in selected building projects, criteria for artist and
site selection and other policies relevant to the public arts program. Such
policies should reflect the following three (3) priorities:
       1.   Community accessibility to the arts;
       2.   Artist accessibility to resources; and
       3.   Opportunities for collaboration and partnerships.
    D.   To review relevant proposals and assist in the process by which
artists, arts organizations, community organizations, businesses, developers,
merchant associations, charitable foundations, or any other member of the
general public proposes and creates projects in the arts which are located in
public places owned and maintained by proposed special events for the village
of Oak Lawn.
    E.   To approve proposals that are not permanently placed on municipal
property for special events which are to be recommended to the Village Board.
    F.   To research and seek additional funding including donations, grants,
and other support to further expand public arts programs special events.
    G.   To encourage public participation in local artistic and cultural
special events and programs.
    H.   To cooperate with other public and private entities regarding the arts
special events.
    I.   To increase artistic recognition through exhibitions and/or
competitions.
    J.   To provide leadership and a voice for the arts in Oak Lawn and to
advocate for the arts in both public and private endeavors.
    K.   To offer educational programming to the public regarding the arts and
to coordinate events and outreach related to the arts.
    LI.   The powers and duties of the Arts and Special Events Commission shall
be to determine when and where events and parades are to be held in the
village, the type of special event or parade, those who shall participate
therein, to set out where the special events are to be held or the parade
routes, and to provide crowd and traffic control in consultation with the
village police department. 
 
 
 
SECTION 7:   That Title 2, Chapter 21, Section 7 of the Oak Lawn Village Code
is hereby amended as follows (additions to existing text marked with underlined
text ; deletions to existing text marked using strikethrough ):
2-21-7:  PUBLIC ARTS FUND:RESERVED
A public arts fund is hereby created to serve as an account through which funds
from the village, outside grant monies, private and corporate donations for the
arts, and other revenue sources can be received, collected, and distributed.
 
   SECTION 8: Any policy, resolution, or ordinance of the Village that
conflicts with the provisions of this Ordinance shall be and is hereby repealed
to the extent of such conflict.
 
   SECTION 9: This Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and after
its passage and approval in the manner provided by law.
 
PASSED THIS this 14th day of October, 2025.
 
   AYES: Trustees Olejniczak, Mallo, Stalker, and Soch
   NAYS:    
   ABSENT: Trustees Pembroke and Desmond
 
APPROVED THIS 14th day of October, 2025.
 
            ______________________________________________________
                     VILLAGE PRESIDENT
 
ATTEST:
 
