in pamphlet form by authority of the President and Board of Trustees of the
Village of Oak Lawn
 
 
ORDINANCE NO. 25-16-59
 
AN ORDINANCE AMENDING TITLE 11 (MOTOR VEHICLES AND TRAFFIC), CHAPTER 2 (GENERAL
PROVISIONS) AND CHAPTER 9 (BICYCLES/TRICYCLES, LOW-SPEED ELECTRIC BICYCLES, AND
ELECTRIC SCOOTERS)
OF THE OAK LAWN VILLAGE CODE RELATIVE TO PENALTIES FOR THE UNLAWFUL OPERATION
OF BICYCLES/TRICYCLES, LOW-SPEED ELECTRIC BICYCLES AND ELECTRIC SCOOTERS WITHIN
THE VILLAGE OF OAK LAWN
 
WHEREAS, Section 6(a) of Article VII of the 1970 Constitution of the State of
Illinois provides that any municipality which has a population of more than
25,000 is a home rule unit, and the Village of Oak Lawn, Cook County, Illinois,
with a population in excess of 25,000 is, therefore, a home rule unit and,
pursuant to the provisions of said Section 6(a) of Article VII, may exercise
any power and perform any function pertaining to its government and affairs,
including, but not limited to, the power to tax and to incur debt; and
 
WHEREAS, the Illinois Vehicle Code (“Vehicle Code”), 625 ILCS 5/1-100 et seq.,
provides a regulatory framework concerning the use of low-speed electric
bicycles and electric scooters; and
 
WHEREAS, on September 9, 2025, the President and Board of Trustees of the
Village of Oak Lawn adopted Ordinance Number 25-14-46 amending the Oak Lawn
Village Code (“Village Code”) relative to low-speed electric bicycles and
electric scooters and other related changes; and
 
WHEREAS, the Village, pursuant to its home rule powers, deems it necessary to
amend Title 11 (Motor Vehicles and Traffic), Chapter 2 (General Provisions), of
the Village Code to further provide for the regulation of low-speed electric
bicycles, electric scooters, and related devices within the Village; and
 
WHEREAS, the President and Board of Trustees of the Village of Oak Lawn find
and declare that it is in the best interest of the Village and its residents to
revise and amend Title 11 (Motor Vehicles and Traffic), Chapter 2 (General
Provisions), of the Village Code, as provided herein.
 
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED BY THE VILLAGE PRESIDENT AND BOARD OF TRUSTEES
OF THE VILLAGE OF OAK LAWN, COOK COUNTY, ILLINOIS, AS FOLLOWS:
 
SECTION ONE :   The foregoing recitals shall be and are hereby incorporated as
findings of fact as if said recitals were fully set forth herein.
 
SECTION TWO :   Title 11 (Motor Vehicles and Traffic), Chapter 2 (General
Provisions), Section 11-2-16 (Use of Electric Scooters, Class 3 Low-Speed
Electric Bicycles, Low-Speed Gas Bicycles, Prohibited Electric Vehicles,
Coasters, Roller Skates, and Toy Vehicles Restricted) of the Oak Lawn Village
Code is hereby amended to read in its entirety as follows, with additions
underlined and deletions stricken through:
 
“11-2-16: USE OF ELECTRIC SCOOTERS, CLASS 3 LOW-SPEED ELECTRIC BICYCLES, LOW-
SPEED GAS BICYCLES, PROHIBITED ELECTRIC VEHICLES, COASTERS, ROLLER SKATES, AND
TOY VEHICLES RESTRICTED:
A. It shall be unlawful for any person upon skates, a coaster, sled or other
toy vehicle, to go upon any street, highway or roadway other than at a
crosswalk.
B. Pursuant to 625 ILCS 5/11-1518(a), it shall be unlawful for any person to
operate a low-speed electric scooter within the Village.
C. It shall be unlawful for any person upon any electric scooter not included
in the definition of low-speed electric scooter to go upon any street, highway
or roadway with a posted speed limit in excess of 35 mph, other than at a
crosswalk, unless permitted by Illinois law and the vehicle is properly titled
and registered in Illinois, and unless he or she is sixteen (16) years of age
or older and possesses a valid driver’s license.
D. It shall be unlawful for any person under the age of sixteen (16) to be upon
any electric scooter not included in the definition of low-speed electric
scooter on any street, highway or roadway other than at a crosswalk.
E. It shall be unlawful for any person under the age of sixteen (16) to be upon
a Class 3 low-speed electric bicycle on any street, highway or roadway other
than at a crosswalk.
F. It shall be unlawful for any person upon an electric personal assistive
mobility device to go upon any street, highway or roadway other than at a
crosswalk., or to operate any electric personal assistive mobility device on a
sidewalk at speeds greater than eight (8) miles per hour.
G. It shall be unlawful for any person under the age of sixteen (16) to be upon
a low-speed gas bicycle upon any street, highway or roadway and/or on any
sidewalk.
H. It shall be unlawful for any person to operate a low-speed gas bicycle at a
speed greater than 20 miles per hour upon any street, highway or roadway, or to
operate any low-speed gas bicycle on any sidewalk.
I. When at a crosswalk, vehicles under this section shall be walked and not
ridden.
J. It shall be unlawful for the parent of any child or the guardian of any ward
to authorize or knowingly permit any child or ward to violate any provision of
this Section.
K. Fines: Any person who violates any provision of this Section shall be deemed
to have committed a petty offense and shall be fined pursuant to the following
provisions:
1. The first violation of this Section shall be punishable by a fine of not
less than one hundred dollars ($100.00).
2. A second violation of this Section by the same person within a twelve-month
period shall be punishable by a fine of no less than two hundred fifty dollars
($250.00).
3. A third or subsequent violation of this Section by the same person within a
twelve-month period shall be punishable by a fine of no less than seven hundred
fifty dollars ($750.00).
L. Impoundment: In the event any minor violates any provision of this Section
by unlawfully operating any electric scooter, electric bicycle, low-speed gas
bicycle, or any other such device, the Oak Lawn Police Department shall have
the authority to impound such device. Any device impounded under this Section
shall only be released to the owner of the device, if 18 years of age or older,
or to the parent or guardian of a minor owner, after any applicable citations
have been issued by the Village.
(1951 Code 14-8-57)”
SECTION THREE :   That Title 11 (Motor Vehicles and Traffic), Chapter 2
(General Provisions), Section 11-2-19 (Enforcement, Violations, Penalties),
Subsection 11-2-19(C) (Penalty Established) of the Oak Lawn Village Code is
hereby amended to read in its entirety as follows, with additions underlined
and deletions stricken through:
 
“  C.   Penalty Established: Every person convicted of a violation of any of
the provisions of this chapter shall be punished as provided in subsections F
and G of this section and outlined in this title, unless otherwise provided
therein .”
SECTION FOUR : That Title 11 (Motor Vehicles and Traffic), Chapter 9 (Bicycles/
Tricycles, Low-Speed Electric Bicycles, and Electric Scooters), Article A.
(Bicycles/Tricycles), Section 11-9A-11 (Operation Requirements and
Restrictions, Compliance with Laws, Obedience to Traffic Signs), of the Oak
Lawn Village Code is hereby amended to read in its entirety as follows, with
additions underlined and deletions stricken through:
“11-9A-11: OPERATION REQUIREMENTS AND RESTRICTIONS, COMPLIANCE WITH LAWS,
OBEDIENCE TO TRAFFIC SIGNS:
A.   Compliance with Traffic Laws, Regulations: Every person operating a
bicycle/tricycle in the Village shall conform to the provisions of the Illinois
Vehicle Code and shall also be subject to the regulations of this Section.
B.   Riding Abreast: When two (2) or more persons in a group are operating
bicycles/tricycles, they shall not ride abreast but shall ride single file.
C.   Keep to Right: All bicycles/tricycles shall be operated as near to the
right-hand curb as conditions will permit, exercising due care when passing a
standing vehicle or one proceeding in the same direction.
D.   Emerging from Alley, Driveway, Garage: Any person operating a bicycle/
tricycle emerging from an alley, driveway or garage, shall stop the bicycle/
tricycle immediately prior to driving onto or across a sidewalk or onto or
across a sidewalk line projected across any alley, and shall exercise extreme
care in these cases.
E.   Clinging, Attaching to Moving Vehicles: No person operating a bicycle/
tricycle shall cling to or attach himself to any other moving vehicle.
F.   Attaching Other Vehicles to Bicycles/Tricycles: No bicycle/tricycle shall
have attached to it any other vehicle such as a wagon or sled.
G.   Riding on Sidewalks:
       1.   No person shall ride a bicycle/tricycle on the sidewalk in the
business district.
       2.   Whenever a person is riding a bicycle/tricycle upon a sidewalk
other than in the business district, such person shall yield the right of way
to any pedestrian and shall give audible signal before overtaking and passing
such person.
H.   Pedestrians’ Right of Way: The pedestrian has the right of way over
bicycles/tricycles at all times.
I.   Obstructing Streets, Sidewalk: No bicycle/tricycle shall be left lying
upon any street or sidewalk or in such position as to obstruct or interfere
with the use of any street or sidewalk.
J.   Passengers: No bicycle/tricycle shall be used to carry more persons at one
time than the number for which it is designed and equipped, except that an
adult rider may carry a child securely attached to his person in a backpack or
sling.
K.   Riding “No Hands”, Fancy Riding: No rider of a bicycle/tricycle shall
remove both hands from the handlebars or practice any acrobatic or fancy riding
on any street or sidewalk.
L.   Hand Signals: Proper hand signals should be used at all times.
M.   Carrying Articles: No person operating a bicycle/tricycle shall carry any
package, article or bundle which prevents the rider from keeping both hands on
the handlebars or obstructs his vision.
N.   Obedience to Traffic Signs: Every person operating a bicycle/tricycle must
obey all traffic signs.
O. The parent of any child and the guardian of any ward shall not authorize or
knowingly permit any child or ward to violate any provision of this Chapter.
P. Fines: Any person who violates any provision of this Section shall be deemed
to have committed a petty offense and shall be fined pursuant to the following
provisions:
1. The first violation of this Section shall be punishable by a fine of not
less than one hundred dollars ($100.00).
2. A second violation of this Section by the same person within a twelve-month
period shall be punishable by a fine of no less than two hundred fifty dollars
($250.00).
3. A third or subsequent violation of this Section by the same person within a
twelve-month period shall be punishable by a fine of no less than seven hundred
fifty dollars ($750.00).
Q. Impoundment: In the event any minor operating a bicycle/tricycle violates
any provision of this Section, the Oak Lawn Police Department shall have the
authority to impound such device. Any device impounded under this Section shall
only be released to the owner of the device, if 18 years of age or older, or to
the parent or guardian of a minor owner, after any applicable citations have
been issued by the Village.
(Ords. 213, 93-18-74, 94-19-80)”
SECTION FIVE : That Title 11 (Motor Vehicles and Traffic), Chapter 9 (Bicycles/
Tricycles, Low-Speed Electric Bicycles, and Electric Scooters), Article B.
(Low-Speed Electric Bicycles) of the Oak Lawn Village Code is hereby amended by
adding Section 11-9B-4 to read in its entirety as follows:
“ 11-9B-4: FINES AND IMPOUNDMENT:
A. Fines: Any person who violates any provision of this Article shall be deemed
to have committed a petty offense and shall be fined pursuant to the following
provisions:
1. The first violation of this Article shall be punishable by a fine of not
less than one hundred dollars ($100.00).
2. A second violation of this Section by the same person within a twelve-month
period shall be punishable by a fine of no less than two hundred fifty dollars
($250.00).
3. A third or subsequent violation of this Section by the same person within a
twelve-month period shall be punishable by a fine of no less than seven hundred
fifty dollars ($750.00).
B. Impoundment: In the event any minor operating a low-speed electric bicycle
violates any provision of this Article, the Oak Lawn Police Department shall
have the authority to impound such device. Any device impounded under this
Section shall only be released to the owner of the device, if 18 years of age
or older, or to the parent or guardian of a minor owner, after any applicable
citations have been issued by the Village. ”
SECTION SIX :   That Title 11 (Motor Vehicles and Traffic), Chapter 9
(Bicycles/Tricycles, Low-Speed Electric Bicycles, and Electric Scooters),
Article C. (Electric Scooters) of the Oak Lawn Village Code is hereby amended
by adding Section 11-9C-4 to read in its entirety as follows:
“ 11-9C-4: FINES AND IMPOUNDMENT :
A. Fines: Any person who violates any provision of this Article shall be deemed
to have committed a petty offense and shall be fined pursuant to the following
provisions:
1. The first violation of this Article shall be punishable by a fine of not
less than one hundred dollars ($100.00).
2. A second violation of this Section by the same person within a twelve-month
period shall be punishable by a fine of no less than two hundred fifty dollars
($250.00).
3. A third or subsequent violation of this Section by the same person within a
twelve-month period shall be punishable by a fine of no less than seven hundred
fifty dollars ($750.00).
B. Impoundment: In the event any minor operating an electric scooter, including
a low-speed electric scooter, violates any provision of this Article, the Oak
Lawn Police Department shall have the authority to impound such device. Any
device impounded under this Section shall only be released to the owner of the
device, if 18 years of age or older, or to the parent or guardian of a minor
owner, after any applicable citations have been issued by the Village. ”
SECTION SEVEN :   Any policy, resolution or ordinance of the Village that
conflicts with the provisions of this Ordinance shall be and is hereby repealed
to the extent of such conflict.
 
SECTION EIGHT :    This Ordinance shall be in full force and effect from and
after its adoption and approval in the manner provided by law.
 
ADOPTED this 14th day of October, 2025, pursuant to a roll call vote as
follows:
 
   AYES: Trustees Olejniczak, Mallo, Stalker, and Soch
   NAYS:    
   ABSENT: Trustees Pembroke and Desmond
 
 
APPROVED by me this 14th day of October, 2025 and attested by the Village Clerk
on the same day.
 
    
_______________________________
                         Village President
ATTEST:
 
 
